        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I came to this from `lightspeed.nvim`. I didn't expect to only be able to jump to beginnings or ends of words at first; I realized that doesn't really matter since you can just use `mini.jump` to get to an exact position after a `mini.jump2d`. Feels very fast, even on old hardware",
