        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yes, you correctly interpreted what I meant, with jumps I meant keystrokes. I guess, I got used to the way hop works, so for me I am most often moving around near the current position of the cursor. But as you clearly stated, it is ok to have a different focus for jump2d, it is a valid use case to expect uniformity in the number of keystrokes. You cannot make everybody happy, otherwise it wouldn‘t be „mini“ anymore ",
